      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Thanks for voicing your concerns, @{5e4ca2145f9b3726b3b389e7|full_name}. I understand how SDK3 and the 3.x.x versioning has become synonymous. We launched the VPM versions of SDK3 at 3.0.0 so that it would be clear to creators that it was still SDK3.\n\nThe current internal Unity-2022-compatible VRChat SDK does have non-backwards-compatible breaking changes due to the move to .NET Standard 2.1 and possibly other factors, so we'll want package creators to test and update their packages to be 4.x.x compatible, and do not want to mix 3.x-compatible and 4.x-compatible packages automatically, which would be much more likely without a major version change.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
